Compiler result: Outside code cannot access the protected helper through ordinary typed access. Diagnostic 2445. This intentionally failing example is separate from the runnable solution.

after:
```typescript
class LabelBase {
  protected prefix(text: string): string {
    return "Topic: " + text;
  }
}
class TopicLabel extends LabelBase {
  render(text: string): string {
    return this.prefix(text);
  }
}
const label = new TopicLabel();
console.log(label.render("Stars"));
```
This prints `Topic: Stars`. `render` passes the text to the inherited helper and returns its result.
